WEBVTT

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.150
We have a message from the Port Control Tower.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:13.240
The Grandcypher, a mid-sized unarmed airship,
is requesting permission to enter

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.570
via the Auguste-Albion Skyway.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.580
Permission granted.
Handle the rest according to plan.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.410
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.830
Make sure to not let me down, understand?

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.710
After all I did to pave the way for you.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.300
Thank you very much.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.930
It astounds me, what a mess you've made.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.230
Well, not that I care what you do,
so long as you stay out of my way.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.110
It's been six years, my dearest Katalina.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.750
So that's the Albion Citadel.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.120
We're finally here.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:30.960
Katalina.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.420
Our future rests on today's negotiations.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:41.340
We're up against the empire.
It's not going to be smooth sailing.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.350
Listen up!

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.980
The secret to negotiating is
to not let your opponent underestimate you!

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.190
If you're a mess on the outside,
you'll be a mess on the inside!

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.850
So we're gonna make you look like a winner!

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:52.690
Right!

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.270
Nobody's afraid of you, bub!

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.570
How was that?

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.910
We have no idea what kind of conditions
they're going to set.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.490
It's entirely possible that
this whole peace talk is a trap.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:11.540
Why confer with us when they could simply
revoke the warrant for our arrest?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.670
Yeah, they don't exactly inspire trust...

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.750
Well...

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.720
You know how the imperial generals are,
each doin' their own thing.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.300
Even if one of 'em has it out for us,
it's not like they all do.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:30.020
We should consider intervention
or conspiracy by a third party.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.440
You mean like the Black Knight in Valtz?

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:42.780
She may be the empire's top advisor,
but her objectives are murky.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:48.660
Still, even if our chances were one in a million,
I would still risk it.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:55.080
As long as it means you and Lyria
can be free, then I would...

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.210
Gran...

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.210
Hey, don't shoulder everything.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.630
If push comes to shove, you've got us.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:05.090
Just think of this as a chance
 to do some sightseeing in Albion.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.300
Don't sweat it.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.900
Wow...

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.660
Amazing!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.170
We've been awaiting your arrival.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.510
Allow me to escort you to the castle.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.450
There you can see Albion Military Academy,
considered to be the city's core.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:13.040
Albion was built around the academy,
making us a university city.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.460
Of course we teach battle techniques
and military theory,

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.630
in addition to history, politics, and etiquette.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.420
Each of our graduates hone many skills here

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:27.970
and set off into the world to find
positions in militaries or royal households.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:35.270
I hear the graduates are sought after
by pretty much everyone.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:37.980
Even by the empire?

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.480
Yep, but not just them.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.570
Guess you could say this place
is neutral in that sense.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.950
So that's why the empire
wanted to have negotiations here.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:49.780
Uh, excuse me...

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.160
It's an honor to meet you, Ms. Katalina.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.830
M-My name is Garcia Schuler.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.500
Oh, is that right?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:05.300
So you're this year's valedictorian.
You must be an outstanding student.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.590
Oh, no! I pale in comparison to you!

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.680
I've heard all about it.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.980
How you and Vira vied for the post
of Lord Commander in an epic showdown!

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:20.020
Now you're exaggerating. I was never that...

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.150
What's he talking about?

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.980
Oh, well... Did I not tell you?

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.570
I actually graduated from this school.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.320
You never told us!

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.580
If only you'd said something,
we could've asked you more about Albion!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:37.960
I see. So this is where Katalina studied.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.880
Well, like they say, everyone has a history.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.130
Really, you need to tell us these things, you know!

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.430
And here I thought we were friends.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:55.430
I'm really sorry.
I never meant to keep it a secret...

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.730
I have been awaiting your arrival.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.400
It's been a long time, Katalina.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.070
Vira...

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:10.950
You know each other?

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.910
My name is Vira Lillie.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.870
I am the Lord Commander of the Albion Citadel.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.330
Lord Commander?

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.210
Wow, and you're so young... Oops, sorry.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.840
I will be observing today's peace negotiations.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.930
I am by no means experienced,
but I look forward to working with you.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:36.680
And with that,
you can all consider yourselves free.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.390
Now you can go wherever you please.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:41.480
Congratulations.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.530
Huh? What's with the lukewarm reaction?
How about looking a little happier?

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.860
I'm not really sure what to say...

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.650
I'm totally confused!

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:55.950
Are you really gonna give up on Lyria
after chasing her down like a madman?

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.500
To be honest, it's getting to be
a hassle, you know?

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:04.630
My men, the lot of fools,
are always getting their butts handed to them.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.590
So I thought it was time to cut my losses.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.510
The empire is willing to relinquish
a top-secret asset for a reason like that?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:16.350
Things have changed since you
were with us, Lieutenant Katalina.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.970
Could you please explain?

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:27.610
To tell the truth, our research on the girl
was about to reach a dead end.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:31.150
Though a few, like Pommern,
stubbornly refused to acknowledge it.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.740
We were able to forcefully draw out
some of her powers,

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.620
but there was still the question of

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:43.290
whether we'd be able to decipher the mechanism
and find a way to actually control it ourselves.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:49.300
No point in throwing copious amounts
of research funding at a dead end, is there?

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.760
Hey! Don't talk about her like that!

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.550
So you'll really back off?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.050
We do have plenty of other options, you see.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.390
Weapons that are far more useful to us, that is.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.980
Here's your letter of pardon.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:11.280
Should our paths cross again,
let's chat over tea, shall we?

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.030
Sounded logical enough, I guess.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:22.950
But we can't just bury the past
and leave it at that.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.580
What do you think?

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:29.460
This letterhead looks official.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.590
But it's hard to believe
the empire would back off without a fight.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.340
Should we believe him?

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:39.760
Are all of us... truly free?

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:42.260
Lyria...

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:48.350
I do believe you can appreciate
the situation for now.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:53.030
Regardless of the empire's intentions,
you've been officially pardoned at the very least.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.740
Vira...

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.990
You all must be exhausted from your long journey.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.870
We do have a modest banquet planned for you.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:04.160
Tonight, please make yourselves
at home in the castle.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.960
That's an offer we can appreciate, but...

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.750
Shall we prepare your clothes
for the banquet, as well?

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:15.880
There's so much catching up
that I'd like to do with you, Katalina.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:27.310
Ta-da!

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.270
Wow!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.900
Clothes really make a difference, huh?

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.270
Ouch!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.730
What the hell?
That was a compliment! That hurts...

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.740
It looks good on you.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.410
The Lord Commander
sure has an eye for fashion.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.620
You actually don't look half bad yourself!

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:47.000
You guys, when are we gonna eat?

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.080
Thank you for your patience.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:11:00.550
Gran... Um...
Does it look strange?

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.890
Not at all! Um...

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.230
What's the big idea?

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:15.400
Jeez! Can't you see a lady's
gotten all dressed up?

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:16.900
Say something, will you?

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.030
Sorry I'm late.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.000
Is that the Albion dress uniform?

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.330
Katalina, you look so cool!

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:36.590
I wasn't sure about it,
since it's been so long since I graduated...

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.010
Oh, who cares? It's a special night!

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:48.720
It is with great pleasure that we welcome
the crew led by Captain Gran tonight.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:53.520
I am truly delighted to report that
the peace negotiations held today

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:59.030
have resulted in the Erste Empire's revocation
of the warrant for their arrest.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:08.410
To the skyfarers who have regained
their freedom in the skies...

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:09.250
Cheers!

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.460
Cheers!

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:40.530
So you and Katalina went to
the academy together, Lord Commander?

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.030
Please call me Vira.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:49.080
Back then, we sat next to each other every day
and trained from morning till night.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.290
That was six whole years ago.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.160
That's right.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.710
So even you were a young student once, huh?

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.250
Good work, Captain!

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:06.840
We're hearing all about Katalina
and Vira's past right now.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:11.600
Katalina was the best student
in the entire school.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:15.560
Scholarship, ability, even etiquette...
She was perfect in every way.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.900
Aren't you talking about yourself, Vira?

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.820
She was the valedictorian,
representing the entire student body,

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.860
and everyone looked up to her...

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:25.990
Including me, of course.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.000
That's all in the past.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:42.670
Every day, her desk would be piled
with letters from her admirers.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:46.590
Well, if you're going to go there,

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:50.970
you had guys dueling each other for the right
to ask you to the Holy Knight Festival.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:56.520
Yet, in the end, I chose to go with you.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:04.940
That's right. I didn't gain many fans
by accepting your invitation.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.320
They must've been really close.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:08.450
Friends, huh? I wonder how Aaron's doing.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.280
Excuse me, ma'am.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.370
Some other guests would like
to speak with you.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:16.710
I'll be right there.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.250
Please, enjoy yourselves.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.310
Why the long face?

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.780
That the one the pipsqueak general came on?

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.820
Hard to believe he'd stick around
with the negotiations wrapped up.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:01.250
You okay? You're not feeling sick, are you?

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:03.540
I'm just taking a breather.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.260
I'm not really cut out
for these kinds of formal events.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:09.680
Hey, you were killin' it!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.800
Absolved and released, huh?

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.020
Are we really off the hook?

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.600
You sure are a worrywart, Gran.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:23.730
It hasn't sunk in yet. I mean...

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:39.000
That's amazing. What's it a picture of?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.500
Good job, Gran!

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.830
Did you want some water or...

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:46.880
Lyria?

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.420
A primal beast.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.260
I've been sensing it this whole time...

00:15:54.680 --> 00:16:01.600
Ever since we got to this island. It's faint,
but I feel it's been watching over us...

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.940
That must be the primal beast,

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:07.730
Luminiera.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.740
Luminiera?

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.360
I knew you would notice.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:15.740
Just what I'd expect
of the empire's greatest secret.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:19.750
Forgive me.

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.500
When I was appointed
to observe the negotiations,

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.960
I was given some details about you.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.170
I see.

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:32.130
Luminiera is a primal beast
who protects Albion and its knights.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:38.060
With her sword,
she offers protection to the knights,

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:40.060
defending the island and its people.

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:45.940
Only the most powerful knight
can become Luminiera's master.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.070
That is why...

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:56.950
The one to lay claim to the title
of Lord Commander has long been decided

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:59.410
by a special martial arts tournament.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.460
And once bonded to Luminiera,

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:13.800
all Lord Commanders must live out their lives
protecting this island, never to leave Albion.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.050
Then that means you, too.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:17.640
Yes.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:21.060
My predecessor fell ill
and passed away six years ago,

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:24.100
and I was chosen as the successor
in a deciding match.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:28.150
Wow, looks sure can be deceiving, huh?

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:32.990
I was simply absorbed in what I was doing.
There were contestants more powerful...

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.610
...than myself.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.660
What are you all doing out here?

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.410
I've been looking for you.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:45.290
Forgive me. We were discussing
Albion's primal beast, you see.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:47.000
Right?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:55.170
I think they'll be serving an Albion specialty,
custard apple pie, any minute now.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.470
Please be sure to try some.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:58.840
Apple pie!

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:01.600
Okay, let's head back.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:05.020
Katalina?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:22.280
Can't eat any more...

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.170
Katalina?

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.960
What's the matter?

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.340
Oh, uh...

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.180
For some reason, I can't sleep.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.640
It was quite the eventful day today.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.730
Do you think we can trust them?

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.400
The empire, you mean?

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:54.190
Eugen said they sounded logical enough.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:59.240
But personally, I just don't see those guys
giving up on Lyria so easily.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.200
I understand how you feel,

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:07.830
but at the same time, we'll never be able
to move forward if we remain suspicious.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.920
We've regained our freedom,
so why not leave it at that?

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:15.460
Now you can continue
on your journey without fear.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:19.380
Shouldn't you just be happy
and focus on the future?

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:26.270
You know, I never thought I'd hear
those words from you, Katalina.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.020
Is that right?

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.980
Do you trust the empire, Katalina?

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.740
The one I trust is...

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:42.740
Gran, it's you.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:45.330
Me?

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:48.410
And Lyria.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:53.960
I know that you two will get there.
To Estalucia, the Island of the Astrals,

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.250
and beyond that,
wherever you want to go.

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:04.390
I'm glad you were the one we ran into
after fleeing the empire.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.140
It's truly a blessing.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.060
Katalina!

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.270
We have another early morning tomorrow.
Good night.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:23.240
Gran! Gran!

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.570
Wake up, Gran!

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:29.580
What's wrong, Lyria?

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:31.410
L-Look...

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:41.170
<i>I've decided to leave the ship.
Forgive me for my selfishness.</i>

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:46.720
<i>I pray your upcoming journey
will be free of misfortune.</i>

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.180
<i>I bid you farewell, Lyria.</i>

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:54.060
<i>Sorry that I couldn't keep my promise.</i>

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:07.150
Orchis!

00:23:21.670 --> 00:23:22.500
Apollo...

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:25.920
Come, doll.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
EPISODE 3
FALSE FREEDOM

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:38.980
Next episode, "False Freedom."
